{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CI evidence addendum — GitHub Actions inspected 2026-08-08\n\nThe live CI record strengthens the external-integration assessment but exposes a material reliability flaw in the default-suite gate.\n\n### Audited SHA / quality-gate status\n- Gerrit Verified run 31269824243 on base SHA 24917e843b1472adc682bcde7a9c2e5a1727acfd succeeded across lint+type-check, pip-audit, artifact provenance, optional-dependency isolation, eval discipline, clean-install golden path, authorship identity, Ubuntu Python 3.11/3.12/3.13, and macOS Python 3.13.\n- Its Ubuntu Python 3.11 cell ran 11,462 passed / 66 skipped at 83.49% coverage, plus 129 passed / 10 skipped in the integration tier.\n- Recent CodeQL SAST: 5/5 green. Optional-Dependency Isolation mirror: 5/5 green. Recent Mirror Guard and Reconciler Heartbeat runs are green. Reconcile Bridge scheduled cancellations are concurrency supersession alongside successful dispatch runs, not job failures.\n\n### Live external evidence\nLatest complete Live External Integration run 30986591446 succeeded with zero skipped jobs:\n- Jira Data Center: 62 passed, 1 xfailed; live canary executed 62/63 collected.\n- Jira live-services/Cloud lane: 17 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed; live canary executed 8/9.\n- Anthropic: 15 passed, 1 skipped; 15/16 live tests executed.\n- Bedrock: 16 passed; 16/16 live tests executed.\n- OpenAI: 15 passed, 1 skipped; 15/16 live tests executed.\n- Langfuse round-trip: 1 passed.\nThis converts the original external-integration conclusion from workflow-design evidence to observed live execution evidence.\n\n### New material finding\nMEDIUM — CI gate reliability: the Python 3.11 xdist worker repeatedly dies in tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py::test_matching_guard_is_accepted with “node down: Not properly terminated,” after roughly 11.4k passing tests. Observed in Gerrit Verified runs 31266912051, 31267701635, 31268737675, and 31269084668, plus scheduled mirror runs 31245335199 and 31258682512. The identical Gerrit 1548 patchset then passed unchanged in run 31269824243, proving flakiness rather than patch behavior. Impact is a spurious Verified-1 and approximately 8–24 minutes of rerun latency per occurrence. Existing open ticket fade-ea90-7564-4715 already tracks the exact failure and proposed teardown/serialization investigation.\n\nRevised test-quality score: 8.0/10 (from 8.5). External coverage and oracle design are excellent; repeatability of the blocking gate is currently below the same standard. Code 7.5, architecture 8.0, and documentation 8.0 remain unchanged."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786213117025551001,"uuid":"820cdd7d-d78e-4946-8728-61fc1a8b39cc"}